##Cooking Efficiency
Prepwise aims to minimize the total time and effort required to prepare multiple meals in one cooking session.
An efficient cooking plan should:
Minimize total elapsed time: Organize cooking tasks to reduce the time from starting meal preparation to finishing all meals.
Combine preparation tasks: Identify shared ingredients and preparation steps across recipes to avoid unnecessary repeated work or idle wait time.
Coordinate cooking tasks: Schedule independent tasks to occur simultaneously when possible and safe.
Respect user constraints: Account for the user's available cooking time, equipment, serving sizes, and dietary restrictions.
Provide realistic schedules: Use estimated preparation and cooking durations, accounting for tasks that must be completed before others can begin.


##Key Features

MVP
Student accounts: The system allows students to sign up and login to their account.
Preferences: The system should ask a series of questions to determine user preferences such as dietary restrictions, foods to avoid, allergies, etc.
Settings: Users should be able to view and update preferences as necessary
Meal Prep: the app recommends the user a few recipes to use for meal prepping based on preferences set. It should exclude recipes that contain allergies or foods users want to avoid.
Coordinated cooking schedule: The app recommends the most efficient way to complete the cooking session. It should provide an ordered sequence of cooking tasks. Each task must include instructions and an estimated duration.
Step-by-Step Cooking schedule: The app gives students clear and concise instructions so they are not overwhelmed.

Post MVP
Grocery List: Generate a grocery list from the selected recipes.
Calendar: Students should be able to plan for multiple weeks in advance and have it displayed on the calendar.
Ingredient Overlap: the app prioritizes recipes that have the same ingredients, helping students reduce grocery costs.

